{
  "schema": 2,
  "name": "Molten Core: ten CoA bots fight Lucifron and his timeline follows the measured kit",
  "contract": [
    "Lucifron 12118 is the real Molten Core spawn (creature guid 56605, map 409,",
    "923.3191/-925.5587/-189.90823, o 5.962888, phaseMask 1; pending_db_world rev_20261001_30, checked in the",
    "slot world database before the runs). His AI is coa_boss_ai, driven by coa_boss_schedule; the Flamewaker",
    "Protector adds are deleted (rev_20260930_98). The ten players are CoA classes at level 60, the Normal",
    "access level (rev_20260930_82): a Barbarian tank and four Barbarian melee with Ancestral Strike 802450",
    "(the level 56 rank, AscensionSpellProgressionData.h) and a Worn Shortsword, two Sun Clerics healing with",
    "Illumination 502429 (level 60 rank) and three Pyromancers casting Flare Bolt 502018 (level 60 rank;",
    "Spell.dbc CastingTimeIndex 19 = SpellCastTimes 2500 ms; SpellRange 35 = 35 yd). They group into one raid before entering, so every member",
    "follows the leader's instance bind (InstanceSaveMgr::PlayerGetDestinationInstanceId); a scenario location",
    "inside the raid would give each ungrouped player its own instance. Phase 1 shows them the real spawns.",
    "They gather 37.8 yd from Lucifron on the floor of his previous spawn (rev_20260930_98, .gps -181.997),",
    "outside his aggro radius; once the tank has engaged, the healers and ranged move onto his spawn point",
    "(teleport_to_spawn), the only other floor position known, so the bots' 40 yd heal and 30 yd ranged limits",
    "reach the whole raid. Lucifron has 588759 health at the base flex tier (coa_boss_flex hp_d0), far beyond",
    "what the bots deal in the window, so the fight ends with a killing blow through the normal death path.",
    "Health fixtures (set_health maximum) keep the tank and the raid alive through the window: they are",
    "calibration, not a claim about real damage: in calibration slot run 20261025T141348198910288Z the tank",
    "kept 96.5 percent of 2,000,000 and every other player at least 89 percent of 500,000 after 80 s.",
    "Asserted, with their independent sources: Shadow of Lucifron 12268 appears within 11 s of the engage: in",
    "combat logs 294, 1289, 1602 and 1734 (coa-log-history) players first hit it 10.08, 10.20, 10.07 and 10.06",
    "s after Lucifron's first log line, so it exists by then (the logs do not show its spawn itself); 11 s is",
    "that bound rounded up. The designed coa_boss_summon row (5000 ms after engage, rev_20260930_92) is",
    "context, not the source. Shadow Bolt 2105212 has a 1500 ms cast (Spell.dbc CastingTimeIndex 16) and the",
    "timeline records a cast when it completes. Combat logs 294, 1289, 1602 and 1734 (coa-log-history) start",
    "it 5.93-5.98 s after Lucifron's first log line and every 15.0-15.1 s (its 2105213 hits follow 1.6-1.7 s",
    "later), matching the 5300/15100 ms schedule within a second; so the first completed cast lands 5.8-7.8 s",
    "after the engage (5300 ms plus the cast time, plus or minus a second of engage and tick jitter) and the",
    "casts repeat every 14.0-16.2 s. Fierce Blow 975011 is cast at least five times and only on the tank: the",
    "four logs show it on one player only (the tank) in every fight, roughly every 7.8 s on average with high",
    "variance, and Spell.dbc gives it melee range (SpellRange 2). Nothing evades during the encounter, and the",
    "kill moves the instance boss state to DONE once. Recorded, not asserted (uncertain expectations, evidence",
    "in the result timeline): Curse of Lucifron 2105206 (schedule 18.8 s first, 79.9 s period; the four logs",
    "start it at 16.6-19.9 s and repeat it every 66.6-70.7 s, except 79.9 s in fight 1289); Suppressing",
    "Shadows 2105218 (schedule 29.2 s first, 25.1 s period; the logs start the cast at 29.9-30.0 s and every",
    "25.0-25.1 s, and only its per-target aura events recur every 1-5 s); Impending Doom 2105201 (schedule",
    "first 20.9-27.5 s, every 22.2-22.6 s, rev_20261005_20, from its 2105205 hits in fights 1289, 1602 and 1734;",
    "fight 1289 alone logs its 2105201 aura, first at 13.3 s and then every 26.5-27.7 s, so the readings",
    "disagree). The bots follow the harness raid roles; the tank's threat floor is a test fixture that keeps the",
    "victim deterministic, not threat realism."
  ],
